---
description: Branch-State-Before-PR
alwaysApply: false
---

Context: Changes in the branch will ultimately be marged into `main` (or other branch if specified by the user) via Pull Request. PR should be easy to review so it should stay at or below 500 line changes. (excluding docs and docstring).

What you should do: Before you do the commit, provide information on the sate of the branch and what line changes we accumulate in the branch at origin (what we already pushed + commits we plan to build now). If 500 line changes is exceeded, don't fail but tell it to user and propose a logical split into multiple PRs.

Important: This rule is not dogmatic. If changes must/should be reviewd together, it's fine to put more lines but still — notify the user on the count.